''[[Gotham (TV series)|Gotham]]'' is an American [[superhero]] [[Police procedural|crime-drama]] television series developed by [[Bruno Heller]], based on characters appearing in and published by [[DC Comics]] in their [[Batman]] [[Batman franchise media|franchise]], primarily those of [[Commissioner Gordon|James Gordon]] and [[Batman|Bruce Wayne]]. The series stars [[Ben McKenzie]] and [[David Mazouz]] respectively as the young [[James Gordon (Gotham)|Gordon]] and [[Bruce Wayne (Gotham)|Wayne]], while Heller executive produces along with [[Danny Cannon]], who also directed the pilot. As originally conceived, the series would have served as a straightforward story of Gordon's early days at the [[Gotham City Police Department]].

